{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For when he sees his children.</b> And the good that I do with the righteous, they will sanctify My name." "<b>They will revere.</b> Others will fear, or it is a participle. After he mentioned Jacob he said by way of parable that if he were alive and were to see the righteous children and the wonder that I will do with them, he together with his sons would sanctify My name, for I am the Holy One of Jacob."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:53.164175358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}